								</td>
							</tr></table></td></tr></table></div>
					<div class="bottom">
					</div>
				</div><a name="28-07-2015" id="28-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						Online BETA Development Report
						<div>
							28-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div style="background: url('images/betaAccessNewsBackground.png') no-repeat;">Resting on laurels is not on the Laboratory's to-do list so last week we soldiered on with performance improvements. This morning we deployed some serious ones along with a bunch of new features.<br>
				<br>
				Performance improvements:
				<ul>
					<li>Major graphics rendering optimisation</li>
					<li>Major memory usage optimisation</li>
				</ul>
				New features:
				<ul>
					<li>Tank names appear at battle start so you know who's who</li>
					<li>Chat bubble appear in game when tanks chat</li>
					<li>Improved username outline (now bright usernames are readable too)</li>
					<li>Tweaked chat colours</li>
					<li>Press Enter from the lobby to start chatting</li>
					<li>Wall of Fame</li>
				</ul><div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#28-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Online BETA Development Report',
							description: 'Resting on laurels is not on the Laboratory\'s to-do list so last week we soldiered on with performance improvements. This morning we deployed some serious ones along with a bunch of new features. Performance improvements: Major graphics rendering optimisation Major memory usage optimisation New features: Tank names appear at battle start so you know who\'s who Chat bubble appear in game when tanks chat Improved username outline (now bright usernames are readable too) Tweaked chat colours Press Enter from the lobby to start chatting Wall of Fame ',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="21-07-2015" id="21-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						TankTrouble Online Delayed
						<div>
							21-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>It should come as no surprise that we will not be ready to unleash TankTrouble Online in June as originally announced...umm, eh, especially since we are now in July. Whichever scientist said June must have had his turret on backwards.<br>
				<br>
				Although Online BETA is looking good and many improvements have already been deployed there is still a great deal of work to be done. Scientists are therefore hesitant to announce a final release date just yet.<br>
				<br>
				Although tank owners have very little patience in regards to destruction we thank you for whatever little you may have.<div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#21-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'TankTrouble Online Delayed',
							description: 'It should come as no surprise that we will not be ready to unleash TankTrouble Online in June as originally announced...umm, eh, especially since we are now in July. Whichever scientist said June must have had his turret on backwards. Although Online BETA is looking good and many improvements have already been deployed there is still a great deal of work to be done. Scientists are therefore hesitant to announce a final release date just yet. Although tank owners have very little patience in regards to destruction we thank you for whatever little you may have.',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="18-07-2015" id="18-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 kickstarter" style="position: relative; margin-top: 105px;"><div>
						Kickstarter Latecomers' Shop Opens
						<div>
							18-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div><img src="images/shopOpens.png" style="position: absolute; left: 250px; top: -135px;"/>Players who were late to the TankTrouble Kickstarter campaign, who crave the great rewards that were offered, and who want to support the development of TankTrouble Online, behold! In the Laboratory's new shop you can get BETA access, tank swag, cool wearables and more! And, the selection will grow concurrently with the continuous development of TankTrouble Online. <a href="?shop">Browse now!</a><div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#18-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Kickstarter Latecomers\' Shop Opens',
							description: 'Players who were late to the TankTrouble Kickstarter campaign, who crave the great rewards that were offered, and who want to support the development of TankTrouble Online, behold! In the Laboratory\'s new shop you can get BETA access, tank swag, cool wearables and more! And, the selection will grow concurrently with the continuous development of TankTrouble Online. Browse now!',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="17-07-2015" id="17-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						First Week of Online BETA Recapped
						<div>
							17-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div style="background: url('images/betaAccessNewsBackground.png') no-repeat;">The Online BETA servers have survived their first week in actual combat. Brave beta testers from around the world and scientists from the Siberian underground have butted barrels in online mazes for the first time. Battles have run largely untroubled with only spasmodic lag. Though there's still lots of room for improvements it has already proven to be good, solid fun!<br>
				<br>
				The scrupulous party of beta testers have searched nooks and crannies for bugs, and while they have added some oddities to the list, they have not been able to crash the servers. Not even once! In fact, it has been a very smooth BETA release (TankTrouble history considering) and we will soon be ready to onboard more beta testers. If you are interested, keep a weather eye on the Kickstarter Latecomers' Shop.<br>
				<br>
				In the coming week the Laboratory will mainly work on performance improvements.<div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#17-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'First Week of Online BETA Recapped',
							description: 'The Online BETA servers have survived their first week in actual combat. Brave beta testers from around the world and scientists from the Siberian underground have butted barrels in online mazes for the first time. Battles have run largely untroubled with only spasmodic lag. Though there\'s still lots of room for improvements it has already proven to be good, solid fun! The scrupulous party of beta testers have searched nooks and crannies for bugs, and while they have added some oddities to the list, they have not been able to crash the servers. Not even once! In fact, it has been a very smooth BETA release (TankTrouble history considering) and we will soon be ready to onboard more beta testers. If you are interested, keep a weather eye on the Kickstarter Latecomers\' Shop. In the coming week the Laboratory will mainly work on performance improvements.',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="10-07-2015" id="10-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						Online BETA Opened
						<div>
							10-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div style="background: url('images/betaAccessNewsBackground.png') no-repeat;">Today is an important milestone in the development of TankTrouble Online (and in the history of destruction in general) as we open Online BETA to the brave beta testers. We would never have made it this far without your encouraging support and unwavering enthusiasm. The Laboratory pays you homage.<br>
				<br>
				As the unsullied, untested servers have never seen real combat and are oblivious to the unrivalled destruction about to descend on them, we must vigilantly ease them into battle. That is why only a small party of beta testers can access ...for now!<br>
				<br>
				Non-believers, infidels and impatient tank owners, rest assured! There are no flying pigs in the Laboratory and though it is cold in the Siberian underground it has not yet frozen! Nonetheless, Online BETA is open!<br>
				<br>
				<div style="background-color: #dddddd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px;">
					Important note: Only players who pledged for beta access during the TankTrouble Kickstarter campaign can access g. Players who missed the Kickstarter will be able to purchase access in the soon-to-open Kickstarter Latecomers' Shop.
				</div><div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#10-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Online BETA Opened',
							description: 'Today is an important milestone in the development of TankTrouble Online (and in the history of destruction in general) as we open Online BETA to the brave beta testers. We would never have made it this far without your encouraging support and unwavering enthusiasm. The Laboratory pays you homage. As the unsullied, untested servers have never seen real combat and are oblivious to the unrivalled destruction about to descend on them, we must vigilantly ease them into battle. That is why only a small party of beta testers can access ...for now! Non-believers, infidels and impatient tank owners, rest assured! There are no flying pigs in the Laboratory and though it is cold in the Siberian underground it has not yet frozen! Nonetheless, Online BETA is open! Important note: Only players who pledged for beta access during the TankTrouble Kickstarter campaign can access g. Players who missed the Kickstarter will be able to purchase access in the soon-to-open Kickstarter Latecomers\' Shop. ',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="09-07-2015" id="09-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						Everything You Need to Know About Online BETA
						<div>
							09-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>Online BETA is "just" the first, early test of TankTrouble Online. Many features are still in development and brave beta testers are expected to encounter oddities as they daringly venture into online mazes to help locate bugs and suggest improvements. Therefore, we need to carefully gauge the number of beta players to avoid crashing the servers while we are still developing. Consequently, only players who pledged for beta access during the Kickstarter campaign will have access ...for now!<br>
				<br>
				Players who missed the Kickstarter but simply must have beta access, fear not! You will be able to purchase access in the soon-to-open Kickstarter Latecomers' Shop.<br>
				<br>
				When we are ready to release TankTrouble Online, everyone will have access.<br>
				<br>
				<div style="background-color: #dddddd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px;">
					<div class="text large" style="text-align: center;">
						Online BETA features
					</div>
					<br>
					Tomorrow:
					<ul>
						<li>Online Battles - sweet bananas!</li>
						<li>Servers in USA, Europe and East Asia</li>
						<li>In-game chat system - shoot first, chat later</li>
						<li>New improved tank design prepped for accessories extravaganza</li>
						<li>A groovy TankTrouble tune straight from the depths of the Siberian underground</li>
					</ul>
					In development:
					<ul>
						<li>Developers' forum for beta players</li>
						<li>Tankcessories (including the exclusive Beta accessory box)</li>
						<li>Mobile and tablet support</li>
						<li>Multiplayer on the same computer</li>
						<li>New score and experience system</li>
					</ul>
					Not forgotten but postponed for now:
					<ul>
						<li>Weapons (all weapons need to be rebuilt from scratch and we will do that in time - for now smooth online battles is our highest priority)</li>
						<li>Laika - the beloved and infamous space dog</li>
					</ul>
				</div><div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#09-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Everything You Need to Know About Online BETA',
							description: 'Online BETA is \"just\" the first, early test of TankTrouble Online. Many features are still in development and brave beta testers are expected to encounter oddities as they daringly venture into online mazes to help locate bugs and suggest improvements. Therefore, we need to carefully gauge the number of beta players to avoid crashing the servers while we are still developing. Consequently, only players who pledged for beta access during the Kickstarter campaign will have access ...for now! Players who missed the Kickstarter but simply must have beta access, fear not! You will be able to purchase access in the soon-to-open Kickstarter Latecomers\' Shop. When we are ready to release TankTrouble Online, everyone will have access. Online BETA features Tomorrow: Online Battles - sweet bananas! Servers in USA, Europe and East Asia In-game chat system - shoot first, chat later New improved tank design prepped for accessories extravaganza A groovy TankTrouble tune straight from the depths of the Siberian underground In development: Developers\' forum for beta players Tankcessories (including the exclusive Beta accessory box) Mobile and tablet support Multiplayer on the same computer New score and experience system Not forgotten but postponed for now: Weapons (all weapons need to be rebuilt from scratch and we will do that in time - for now smooth online battles is our highest priority) Laika - the beloved and infamous space dog ',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="08-07-2015" id="08-07-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						Online BETA Launches Friday at 1100 hours UTC
						<div>
							08-07-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>Ever since we blew our optimistic deadline for Online BETA in the end of April we have been swatting enough bugs to make the 8th plague of Egypt look like a picnic. While we regret this delay, we are excited to announce that we finally got the better of them.<br>
				<br>
				<div class="text large" style="text-align: center;">
					Online BETA will launch this Friday at 1100 hours UTC!
				</div>
				<br>
				<div style="background-color: #dddddd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px;">
					Important note: We need to carefully gauge the number of online players while the servers are young in order to not crash them. Therefore, only players who pledged for beta access during the TankTrouble Kickstarter campaign will have access at this time.
				</div><div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#08-07-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Online BETA Launches Friday at 1100 hours UTC',
							description: 'Ever since we blew our optimistic deadline for Online BETA in the end of April we have been swatting enough bugs to make the 8th plague of Egypt look like a picnic. While we regret this delay, we are excited to announce that we finally got the better of them. Online BETA will launch this Friday at 1100 hours UTC! Important note: We need to carefully gauge the number of online players while the servers are young in order to not crash them. Therefore, only players who pledged for beta access during the TankTrouble Kickstarter campaign will have access at this time. ',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="22-05-2015" id="22-05-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						Online Development Status Report
						<div>
							22-05-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>Since the last status update we have been exterminating server bugs. Now the server is ready and eager to be swarmed by a horde of brave beta testers. However, we are still working on a few incomplete and essential features for the game lobby. Like e.g. letting tanks join battles and create new battles.<br>
				<br>
				As we missed our optimistic deadline once already, we won't venture to proclaim a new unleash date. Instead we ask you only to arm yourself with a little patience (although we'll be the first to admit how hard that is!).<br>
				<br>
				<div class="text large" style="text-align: center;">
					BETA is imminent - keep a weather eye on the news!
				</div><div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#22-05-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Online Development Status Report',
							description: 'Since the last status update we have been exterminating server bugs. Now the server is ready and eager to be swarmed by a horde of brave beta testers. However, we are still working on a few incomplete and essential features for the game lobby. Like e.g. letting tanks join battles and create new battles. As we missed our optimistic deadline once already, we won\'t venture to proclaim a new unleash date. Instead we ask you only to arm yourself with a little patience (although we\'ll be the first to admit how hard that is!). BETA is imminent - keep a weather eye on the news! ',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="15-05-2015" id="15-05-2015"></a><div class="news4 kickstarter" style=""><div>
						Kickstarter Latecomers' Shop Opening Soon
						<div>
							15-05-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>Latecomers to the TankTrouble Kickstarter have been pleading with us to make the rewards available again. Therefore, as promised, we are launching a latecomers' shop. All support for the development of online battles is highly appreciated and we are only happy to satisfy merchandise craving tank owners. The shop will be opening soon!<br>
        		<br>
				If you don't know what the TankTrouble Kickstarter is all about you can find out <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1976320862/tanktrouble-online-battles" target="_blank">here</a>. Remember, the Kickstarter has ended! If you want to get your hands on any of the sweet rewards you must wait for the shop to open.<div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#15-05-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Kickstarter Latecomers\' Shop Opening Soon',
							description: 'Latecomers to the TankTrouble Kickstarter have been pleading with us to make the rewards available again. Therefore, as promised, we are launching a latecomers\' shop. All support for the development of online battles is highly appreciated and we are only happy to satisfy merchandise craving tank owners. The shop will be opening soon! If you don\'t know what the TankTrouble Kickstarter is all about you can find out here. Remember, the Kickstarter has ended! If you want to get your hands on any of the sweet rewards you must wait for the shop to open.',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="07-05-2015" id="07-05-2015"></a><div class="news4 standard" style=""><div>
						Online Development Status Report
						<div>
							07-05-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>It comes as no surprise that the online beast is a hard one to rein. Combined with our, TankTrouble Laboratories', never failing optimism when it comes to posing deadlines it has put us slightly behind schedule. We still struggle to weed out a few hard to catch bugs but we are getting excitingly close to unleash BETA.<br>
				<br>
				<div class="text large" style="text-align: center;">
					BETA ACCESS: Just around the corner &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; ONLINE UNLEASH: June
				</div>
				<br>
				We get daily requests from players that missed the Kickstarter campaign for another way to get hold of those great rewards. Fear not! We are setting up a soon-to-be-announced shop for latecomers.<div class='social'>
						<div class='facebook' onclick="FB.ui({
							method: 'feed',
							app_id: '1658540137729309',
							link: 'https://tanktrouble.com/?news#07-05-2015',
  					  		picture: 'https://tanktrouble.com/images/facebookShareDefault.jpg',
							name: 'Online Development Status Report',
							description: 'It comes as no surprise that the online beast is a hard one to rein. Combined with our, TankTrouble Laboratories\', never failing optimism when it comes to posing deadlines it has put us slightly behind schedule. We still struggle to weed out a few hard to catch bugs but we are getting excitingly close to unleash BETA. BETA ACCESS: Just around the corner &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; ONLINE UNLEASH: June We get daily requests from players that missed the Kickstarter campaign for another way to get hold of those great rewards. Fear not! We are setting up a soon-to-be-announced shop for latecomers.',
							caption: 'TankTrouble.com'
						}, function(response){});"><img src='../images/facebookLogoWhite.svg'><div class='caption'>Share</div></div>
					</div></div></div><a name="13-04-2015" id="13-04-2015"></a><div class="news4 kickstarter" style=""><div>
						Kickstarter Rewards Shipping
						<div>
							13-04-2015
						</div>
					</div><div>We have recieved test samples of all the Kickstarter rewards and they just look awesome! So we started shipping the mugs, T-shirts and hoodies today. If you pledged for any of those you can start watching out for the mail man - sweet swag is coming your way!<br>
